__d(function(e,o,a,n,t,s,r){t.exports={banner:"Prototype terms for testers. Not a real agreement. Draft for counsel review.",version:"Version: demo draft, Nov 9, 2026.",sections:[{id:"what",h:"What Woodstock is",p:"This is a prototype, not a real service. Woodstock is a planning and order-preparation app. It is not a registered adviser or dealer, and it does not give personal investment advice. The people and companies in this demo, including planners and bank profiles, are made up unless named as real institutions."},{id:"incharge",h:"You\u2019re in charge",p:"Nothing moves, and nothing is bought or sold, until you approve it, every time. Woodstock prepares orders that follow your own plan and target, and nothing is sent until you approve it, with Face ID, and confirm it in Questrade. Woodstock never trades without your approval."},{id:"accounts",h:"Your accounts",p:"Your investments are held in your own accounts at Questrade Inc., a member of the Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization (CIRO), protected by the Canadian Investor Protection Fund (CIPF) within its limits. Woodstock never holds your money. Woodstock reads your bank and card accounts; in this demo, payday transfers you approve are simulated, and in the real app they would run only through an arrangement you set up with your bank or Questrade."},{id:"estimates",h:"Estimates",p:"Plans, \u201con track\u201d statuses, left-to-spend amounts, refunds and take-home pay are estimates from the numbers you give or connect. They are not guarantees. Tax figures use 2026 federal and Ontario rates and are before workplace deductions; your tax return and pay stub are the real numbers. Goal dates assume you keep adding the amount shown each payday. When you give your pay before tax during setup, take-home is estimated at about 72% of it. Spending this month adds what is recorded so far to what a typical rest of the month would add. Money kept as cash or in a savings fund is projected with no interest or returns. Investment prices are approximate, and gain is value minus what you paid."},{id:"illustrations",h:"Illustrations",p:"Ranges, typical years, rough years and retirement figures are illustrations, not promises. Average returns come from the FP Canada and Institute of Financial Planning 2026 Projection Assumption Guidelines (short-term 2.4%, fixed income 3.2%, Canadian equities 6.3%, U.S. equities 6.4%, international developed 6.6%, emerging 7.5%, inflation 2.1%), blended by each portfolio\u2019s mix, less fund fees. Swings use each portfolio\u2019s published range. The guidelines are meant for long-term planning; using them for shorter periods is Woodstock\u2019s own method. Retirement figures are in today\u2019s dollars, assume about 25 years of withdrawals, and leave out CPP, OAS and workplace pensions. Returns can be lower, and some years fall outside any range shown. Past results don\u2019t predict future results."},{id:"portfolios",h:"Portfolios and holding periods",p:"The four portfolios are general information, the same for everyone, and not a recommendation for you. You choose; Woodstock doesn\u2019t. Holding periods (\u201cgenerally meant for money you won\u2019t need for at least ...\u201d) are Woodstock\u2019s general guide, based on how much each portfolio can swing; the time bands come from the Ontario Securities Commission (GetSmarterAboutMoney.ca). They are not advice about your situation. You can change your portfolio any time in Money; nothing is bought or sold until you approve it."},{id:"own",h:"Build my own",p:"If you build your own mix, you choose every holding; Woodstock doesn\u2019t review or recommend investments, and its fund list is a sample, not a selection. A single company\u2019s stock can rise or fall much more than a fund. U.S.-listed holdings are bought in U.S. dollars, and Questrade converts at a fee."},{id:"shortterm",h:"Where short-term money is kept",p:"Short-term goals start in a savings fund (a high-interest savings ETF). Woodstock sets this starting choice, the same for every short-term goal and everyone; it isn\u2019t a recommendation for you. Savings funds, money market funds and bond funds are not covered by CDIC and can lose value. GICs are usually covered by CDIC within its limits. You can change where any goal is kept at any time. A savings fund\u2019s price moves very little and its interest can change. Nothing is bought until you approve it, and you can choose uninvested cash instead."},{id:"nonreg",h:"Non-registered accounts and swap-based funds",p:"In a non-registered account, each portfolio uses swap-based funds (Global X Corporate Class ETFs: HXS, HXT, HXDM, HBB and HSAV) in place of the registered funds, with the same weights, the same for everyone. Swap-based funds rely on a contract with a bank, and their tax treatment depends on rules that can change. These funds get the market\u2019s return from a swap, a contract with a bank (for HXDM, National Bank of Canada), and hold cash as collateral. If the bank couldn\u2019t pay, the fund could lose value. Because the fund is a class of a corporation, it may still pay some taxable distributions, and tax rules for these funds have changed before. HXT follows the S&P/TSX 60, not the broader index XIC follows; HXDM follows a futures-roll version of its index. Fund fees plus trading costs are shown on each fund\u2019s page (HXS: MER 0.11%, trading costs 0.46%, as of Aug 21, 2026)."},{id:"talk",h:"Talk it through and the portfolio chat",p:"These are automated, not people, and hold no planning or advising title. They plan with your numbers and explain; they can\u2019t pick investments, file taxes or give legal advice. Answers can be wrong; check anything important with a professional.\nWhen live chat is on, your messages and the plan figures needed to answer them are sent to Woodstock\u2019s chat server and to an AI provider (Anthropic) to write a reply. Replies are checked against Woodstock\u2019s rules before you see them, and some are replaced with a standard answer. Answers can be wrong; check anything important. If live chat isn\u2019t available, you get Woodstock\u2019s built-in answers."},{id:"planners",h:"Planners",p:"Planner calls are with people who hold the CFP or QAFP credential and cover financial planning only, not investment selection. In this demo, planners are examples and no booking is made. Prices shown are illustrative and paid to the planner."},{id:"paid",h:"How Woodstock is paid",p:"Woodstock is paid only by your subscription. It receives no payment from Questrade, from any fund company (including Vanguard, iShares, BMO and Global X), or per trade or per account."},{id:"subscription",h:"Subscription",p:"Free for your first 30 days. After that, $15 a month plus tax ($16.95 in Ontario), billed through your Apple account monthly until you cancel. You can cancel any time in your iPhone\u2019s Settings, under your Apple ID, Subscriptions; Woodstock\u2019s Settings has a link there. Cancel at least a day before the free month ends and you pay nothing. Apple\u2019s terms apply to the payment. In this demo, nothing is charged."},{id:"privacy",h:"Privacy",p:"This prototype keeps your entries on this device only. Clearing the app\u2019s data removes them. Demo sign-in passwords are never saved or sent. If you add your birth year, only the year is kept, on this device, and it is used only for age rules. Don\u2019t enter real account numbers or passwords.\nThe one exception is chat: your messages and the plan figures needed for a reply are sent to Woodstock\u2019s chat server and to Anthropic to produce the reply. Woodstock\u2019s server doesn\u2019t keep them. Anthropic\u2019s own data terms apply to the request. Don\u2019t type passwords, account numbers or other sensitive details into the chat.\nIn a real service, Woodstock would read balances, transactions and holdings from accounts you connect, to build and track your plan, under a full privacy policy."},{id:"demo",h:"Demo mode",p:"This is a demonstration. Data is sample data, approvals and transfers are simulated, and nothing is sent to Questrade, any bank, Apple or a card network. Labels marked \u201c(demo)\u201d show simulated events."},{id:"contact",h:"Contact and version",p:"This is a prototype by Connor Luciani for invited testers. It is not a company offering services. Feedback: through the person who invited you."}]}},839,[]);
